note N1 says 12000 cents, but since it's handwritten and not spoken, it's not a fact. However, the problem says to preserve independent undertakings. Wait, the handwritten note is a separate account, so it's mentioned in the review section but not as a fact.\n\nThe user instructions say to cite whole transcript turns using T references. So T1 is the transcript reference. The handwritten note is N1, but it's not a spoken fact. So in the summary, the supported point is from T1: Support costs 120 dollars.\n\nWait, but the handwritten note says 12000 cents. The problem says not to convert or infer. So 120 dollars vs. 12000 cents. 120 dollars is 12000 cents, but the instructions say not to perform conversions. So even though they're equivalent, I shouldn't say they're the same. So the transcript says dollars, the note says cents. So the summary should have the transcript's 120 dollars as the supported fact, and the handwritten note is a separate entry in the review.\n\nThe review section should show both the transcript and the notes. The problem says to show relevant written and spoken passages together through references. So in the review, list T1 and N1.\n\nNow, the schema requires sections: summary, decisions, actions, review. Each with items. The items need readable text and source references.\n\nFor summary: The supported fact is T1. So \"Support costs 120 dollars.\" (from T1). The handwritten note is separate, so it's in the review.\n\nDecisions: The problem says to list suggested decisions. But in the input, there's no decision mentioned. The transcript is just stating a fact. So maybe no decisions here. But the schema requires the section. If there are no decisions, the items should be empty. Wait, the instructions say \"empty sections have empty items, notice and review_sources, with state draft.\" So if there's no decision, the decisions section should have empty items.\n\nSimilarly for actions. The input doesn't mention any actions, so actions would be empty.\n\nReview section: Need to include both T1 and N1. The problem says to show them together with a notice. So the review items would reference T1 and N1, and note that the handwritten note is separate.\n\nWait, the problem says \"In the review section, show relevant written and spoken passages together through references and a specific notice where useful.\" So the review should have an item that lists T1 and N1 with a notice that they are separate accounts.\n\nSo the review item would be: \"Spoken fact: T1 (Support costs 120 dollars). Handwritten note: N1 (Support costs 12000 cents). Note: Handwritten notes are separate from spoken facts and do not create obligations.\"\n\nBut the problem says not to decide they agree or conflict. So just present both.\n\nNow, check if all required fields are present. The schema has sections: summary, decisions, actions, review. Each with items. The items need to have text and sources.\n\nFor summary: item text is \"Support costs 120 dollars.\" sources: [\"T1\"]\n\nDecisions: empty items.\n\nActions: empty items.\n\nReview: item text would be the notice about T1 and N1, sources: [\"T1\", \"N1\"]\n\nWait, the problem says \"Cite whole transcript turns using their T references.\" So in the summary, the sources should be [\"T1\"].\n\nThe review section should have the sources as [\"T1\", \"N1\"].\n\nAlso, the problem says \"Preserve independent undertakings and agreements.\" But there's no agreement here, just a statement.\n\nCheck if the handwritten note is considered a separate account. The problem states \"Handwritten notes may guide emphasis, but are a separate account: they cannot create spoken facts or obligations.\" So the note is separate, so in the review, we mention both but note they are separate.\n\nSo the review item should state both references and note that the handwritten is separate.\n\nNow, check the JSON structure. The output must be a JSON matching the schema. The schema has sections with items. Each item has text and sources.\n\nSo for summary:\n\n{\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Support costs 120 dollars.\",\n        \"sources\": [\"T1\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nDecisions and actions would have empty items.\n\nReview:\n\n{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Spoken fact: T1 (Support costs 120 dollars). Handwritten note: N1 (Support costs 12000 cents). Note: Handwritten notes are separate from spoken facts and do not create obligations.\",\n        \"sources\": [\"T1\", \"N1\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nWait, but the problem says \"Do not decide that they agree, conflict, are equivalent, or resolve one another.\" So the text should just state both without comment on their relation. So the text should be \"T1: Support costs 120 dollars. N1: Support costs 12000 cents. Note: Handwritten notes are separate from spoken facts.\"\n\nYes, that's better. So the text in the review item is just stating both, with a note that they're separate.\n\nNow, check if all required fields are present. The schema requires the sections to be present, even if empty. So decisions and actions will have empty items.\n\nAlso, the problem says \"empty sections have empty items, notice and review_sources, with state draft.\" So for decisions and actions, the items array is empty.\n\nWait, the schema example in the problem statement shows that sections have items. So if there are no items, the items array is empty.\n\nSo the final JSON should have:\n\n- summary: with one item referencing T1\n- decisions: empty items\n- actions: empty items\n- review: with one item referencing T1 and N1\n\nNow, check the input data again. The transcript has T1 as \"Support costs 120 dollars.\" The handwritten note N1 is \"Support costs 12000 cents.\" So the review item should list both.\n\nAlso, the problem says \"Use supported names only; do not guess who an unnamed speaker is.\" Here, the speaker is Sam in both T1 and N1, but the schema doesn't require speaker names, just the references.\n\nSo the JSON should be structured as per the schema.\n\nLet me make sure there are no other sections. The schema provided in the problem has the sections: summary, decisions, actions, review.\n\nSo the output JSON should have those four sections, each with items (possibly empty).\n\nNow, check if the timestamp in the sources is used. The problem says to keep timing/condition qualifiers, but in this case, the transcript has a timestamp, but the summary doesn't need to include it. The sources are just the T references.\n\nSo the final JSON should look like:\n\n{\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Support costs 120 dollars.\",\n        \"sources\": [\"T1\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"decisions\": {\n    \"items\": []\n  },\n  \"actions\": {\n    \"items\": []\n  },\n  \"review\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"T1: Support costs 120 dollars. N1: Support costs 12000 cents. Note: Handwritten notes are separate from spoken facts and do not create obligations.\",\n        \"sources\": [\"T1\", \"N1\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nWait, the problem says \"Cite whole transcript turns using their T references.\" So in the summary, the sources are [\"T1\"], which is correct.\n\nIn the review, the sources are [\"T1\", \"N1\"], which is correct.\n\nThe text in the review item should not say \"Spoken fact\" but just list the references as per the problem's instruction to not infer. So \"T1: ... N1: ...\" is better.\n\nAlso, the note about handwritten notes being separate is required.\n\nCheck if the problem says \"specific notice where useful.\" So the note is part of the text.\n\nYes, the text includes \"Note: Handwritten notes are separate from spoken facts and do not create obligations.\"\n\nNow, check if all required fields are present. The schema expects the sections to be present, even if empty.\n\nSo the JSON should be as above.\n\nWait, the problem says \"Return only JSON matching the suppli